   "etymology": "Uncertain; perhaps from Proto-Albanian:\n* *jāgnja, from *jaga (whence gjah (“a hunt, chase”)) + *-nja, from Proto-Indo-European *h₁yoǵʰ-ó-s, from metathesized *h₁eyǵʰ- (“to desire, long for”) + *-ós;\n* *sāgnja, from *sāgna (whence gjah (“a hunt, chase”)) + *-ja, from Proto-Indo-European *seh₂g-no-s, from *seh₂g- (“to trace, follow”) + *-nós;\n* or *gānja, from Proto-Indo-European *gʷʰén-ye-ti, from *gʷʰen- (“to strike, slay”) + *-yeti.",
